the  lean cuisine all by yourself  what so i gotta sit here and eat dessert  alone like i'm stephen glansberg yes and  if i'm going with like the kimberley  snyder diet advice i usually try  and not do a starch in a protein within  the same meal just because i mean  actually to tell you the truth i don't  stick with that very often i was just  thinking about the burritos and the um  lean cuisines and stuff like that so for  easier digestion you're supposed to kind  of keep your starches and your protein  separate  here we go  again  i guess you can count on a book titled  the beauty detox to peddle a lot of  bogus food combining rules so as i  discuss in my video right here  basically the ass backwards theory  behind food combining is that eating  protein and starches together puts too  much strain on our digestive system  causing a traffic jam so eating them  separately will give our digestive  system a break but  does our digestive system even need a  break no  i mean our digestive system is a  sophisticated well-oiled machine that's  able to multitask the digestion and  absorption of different nutrients from a  variety of different foods and release  the right cocktail of enzymes to do so  plus there's zero evidence to support  the theory behind food combining which  explains why it's exactly just that it's  just a theory so kudos to holly for like  ditching this stupid diet rule and just  enjoying the damn mashed potatoes at  dinner this is what it looks like i got  it all plated up on my marie antoinette  plate this dinner looks awesome and is  perfectly balanced with healthy fats and  protein from the salmon which also has  lots of iron carbs from the mashed  potatoes and fiber and micronutrients  from the broccoli i also want to note  that if salmon and other fatty fish is a  mainstay in like your regular diet then  there's likely no need for the flax oil  supplement on top especially because the  omega-3s in salmon epa and dha are more  biologically active than the ala in the  flax it's usually one of three things  it's either like a handful of this  catalina crunch i love the fruit flavor  i love like the chocolatey flavors and  the cinnamon flavor but the fruit flavor  to me tastes like tricks or fruit loops  so i love a handful of these or the  catalina crunch oreo cookies i'll have  one of those i like the mint ones too i  freeze them or i'll have like a fruit  bar and these do have sugar in it it's  hard to find a bar that's strictly just  fruit but if holly likes these desserts  great but i also just have to call out  that these are all pretty restrained low  calorie desserts and given that we are  seeing a pretty low calorie day overall  restricting one's fun food to like a  single low sugar keto cookie or a  handful of keto cereal feels  unnecessarily rigid so i like that holly  is flexible when it comes to ditching  some of those diet rules like food  combining i would love to see less focus  on lemon water and detox smoothies and  demonizing a 40 calorie fruit bar  because it has sugar in it and more on  just eating enough food to nourish and  support her needs with all that said  what are my overall thoughts on holly's  diet it's just  not enough without saying exact numbers  because ultimately it doesn't matter  let's just say she's consuming the  equivalent of my two-year-old son it's  very very hard to meet your nutritional  needs on so little food which is likely  why all those supplements are having to  be in rotation but no supplement will  give you energy as holly suggests that's  what the og source of energy food is for  calories from food calories from food is  literally the definition of body energy  not a vitamin or micronutrient these  things can all support energy metabolism  but you still need to eat enough  food and while i appreciate that holly  is relatively flexible in terms of not  strictly following the diet advice  housed in that beauty detox book there  still seems to be a tendency towards  following a very restrictive diet  interestingly holly mentioned in the  video that she was dealing with bloating  and as i discussed in my video right  here under eating is actually one of the  top reasons for bloating as it  essentially starves vital organs causing  them to atrophy and work less optimally  and it reduces our digestive outputs  this can naturally trigger a series of  digestive issues including poor gut  motility constipation  gas and you guessed it bloating i've  also got a whole video on gentle  nutrition strategies to help relieve  bloating which you can watch right here  but all of my colleagues who work  specifically in gi nutrition have told  me that when people are under eating  just eating enough calories and making  no other changes is often enough to  drastically improve their digestion and  bloat so hopefully holly gets the memo  and 86 ds the detox diet book in favor  of fueling her body and gut for optimal  health so on that note that's all that i  have for you guys today if you like this  video be sure to give it the thumbs up  leave me a comment below on who or what  i should review next subscribe to the  channel and i'll see you next time on  abby's kitchen bye  [Music]
 

